# fefw-recomp 0.2.13 runtime evidence

Date: 2026-11-25

Host: `X:\fefw-recomp-0.2.13`
Game dump: `E:\FEFW` (the supplied `X:\FEFW\Fire Emblem꞉ Fortune's Weave + Update 1.1.1.nup` extracted dump)
Game build: `DB93B0125F4850601D61C3EDDE012F8EB2ECFE77`, update `131072`
Runtime: `fefw.exe`, 156,793,344 bytes, built by `fefw-launcher.exe --prepare --game E:\FEFW`
Runtime ABI: `nxmod` API 3 (`add_panel` absent)

Command:

```text
cd X:\fefw-recomp-0.2.13
timeout 120 .\fefw.exe --headless --max-seconds 25 --log "X:/fefw-recomp-0.2.13/fefw-trinity-runtime.log"
```

The `timeout` wrapper returned 124 because the process did not finish its own
shutdown within 120 seconds. The runtime log records the actual stop at 25.7
seconds: `boot: max_seconds reached: the guest is still running; ending the
process`. The process was gone afterwards. This is a shutdown-timing limitation
of the headless run, not a plugin initialization failure.

The runtime wrote to the `[log] path` from `fefw.ini` (`fefw.log`); the
`--log` filename was not created, so the lines below come from `fefw.log`.

